Use the transitions from the previous part (the final $|H-T|$ is $|x|-1$ where $x=j+\delta$, $\delta=-3,-1,1,3$ with probabilities $\tfrac18,\tfrac38,\tfrac38,\tfrac18$):
- from $j=0$ to $2$: probability $\tfrac14$;
- from $j=2$ to $2$: $x=3$, probability $\tfrac38$;
- from $j=4$ to $2$: $x=3$, i.e. $\delta=-1$, probability $\tfrac38$;
- from $j=6$ to $2$: $x=3$, i.e. $\delta=-3$, probability $\tfrac18$;
- from $j\ge8$ it is impossible.

Hence $p_m(2)=\tfrac14p_{m-1}(0)+\tfrac38p_{m-1}(2)+\tfrac38p_{m-1}(4)+\tfrac18p_{m-1}(6)$.

**Answer: $b_1=\tfrac14$, $b_2=\tfrac38$, $b_3=\tfrac38$, $b_4=\tfrac18$**
